+<h2>Referral's pool listener, ready hook, milestone, referral-service and fraud-load catches keep logging when the thrown value is unreadable &mdash; KS-1868, referral, TIER 1</h2>
+<div class="note"><table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>What to know.</strong></td><td> Fourteen catches in <code>services/referral/src</code> (the pool listener and ready hook in <code>db.ts</code>, the progress, pending-reward, verify and two write catches in <code>milestoneService.ts</code>, four read catches in <code>referralService.ts</code>, the load catch in <code>fraudDetection.ts</code>) read <code>err.message</code> unguarded. A revoked Proxy or a throwing <code>message</code> getter made that read throw, so the call rejected. Each now logs text, or the constant <code>unreadable thrown value</code>, and takes its ordinary fallback. That fallback is not harmless here: a failed progress read becomes a fresh default and the milestone check awards every qualifying milestone again as CLAIMABLE rewards; a failed fraud load starts the fraud service empty.
+    </td></tr><tr><td>The five edits are held Spark passes O89-P2, O90-P4, O90-P5, O90-P11 and O90-P12, applied strictly and never hand-edited. TIER 1 (Opus gate) for the reward and fraud outcomes.
+    </td></tr></table>
+</div>
+<div class="note"><table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="1"><strong>Not measured here.</strong></td><td> KS-1868 stays open. A real Postgres, a boot on a box, the unguarded reads that remain in <code>referralService.ts</code>, the four platform suites, whole-suite CI and Node 24 were not run.
+    </td></tr></table>
+</div>
+<h3>Running the cells</h3>
+<pre><code>npm --prefix Blockchain/Dev/services/referral test -- src/__tests__/ks1868-milestone-service-db-read-catches-unreadable-throw.test.ts   # 9 cells; four more files hold 32
+npm --prefix Blockchain/Dev/services/referral test                                                                                      # 12 files / 77 cells</code></pre>
+<h3>Figures</h3>
+<table>
+<tr><th>Figure</th><th>Value</th></tr>
+<tr><td>new cells</td><td><strong>41</strong> in 5 files; red first: 26 of 41 failed without the change, all by assertion; 15 controls green</td></tr>
+<tr><td>suite, before then after</td><td>referral 36 then 77 (measured 2026-11-03, Node v26.8.1)</td></tr>
+</table>
